# Local working files (superpowers specs/plans): `.gitignore` excludes them and `.gitattributes`
# keeps them out of release archives, so they are never published.
# Needed beyond `.pi-lens.json`'s `ignore`: pi-lens' autoformat phase does not
# consult that matcher, it shells out to prettier with cwd set to the nearest
# tool-config root (this repo root), so this file is what actually exempts it.
docs/superpowers/

# The same reason applies to `.superpowers/` — SDD workspaces and the agent
# artifacts inside them (task briefs, review packages, experiment runs). They are
# gitignored, never published, and one old workspace alone holds ~480 files of
# captured runs, so without this line a developer with local SDD state sees
# `bun run format:check` fail at the repo root while CI (a clean checkout) stays
# green. Keep this ahead of the markdown rule so the intent reads as one block.
.superpowers/

# Markdown is hand-formatted by policy (AGENTS.md: "Markdown is intentionally
# not gated — hand-format docs"), while pi-lens' deferred autoformat would other-
# wise reflow every edited doc. CI's format:check glob never covered markdown, so
# excluding it here only removes writes the gate never verified.
**/*.md
